  beschreibung: The Sun is not a planet, but the star at the center of our solar
    system. Its gravity keeps planets, moons, asteroids, and comets on their paths.
    Inside the Sun, hydrogen nuclei fuse into helium, releasing the energy that reaches
    Earth as light and heat. Without the Sun, liquid water, weather, and life on
    Earth would not be possible.
  planetSizeInfoText: The Sun is not a planet, but a star. Its diameter is about
    109 times Earth's diameter.
  orbitalDistanceInfoText: The Sun forms the center of the model. For the Sun itself,
    the distance from the Sun is therefore 0 AU.
  orbitalSpeedInfoText: The Sun does not orbit the Sun. This value in the dataset
    does not represent a planetary orbit.
  axialTiltInfoText: The Sun also rotates around an axis, which is slightly tilted
    relative to Earth's orbital plane.
  eccentricityInfoText: As the central star, the Sun has no orbit around the Sun
    in this model.
  planetScaleInfoText: In a size comparison, the Sun towers over all planets. Even
    Jupiter is only about one tenth as wide.
  gravityInfoText: Gravity at the visible surface of the Sun is about 28 times stronger
    than on Earth.
  fakten: []
